# Mutation table for the organize row-writing path, server side.
#
# Format: NAME | FILE | PERL_EXPRESSION      (see scripts/mutation-matrix.sh)
# Run:
#   scripts/mutation-matrix.sh \
#     --pkg ./internal/server/ \
#     --table scripts/mutation-tables/organize-row-writers-server.muts
#
# WHAT THIS TABLE IS FOR. Every mutation below restores one of the four ways
# the organize path used to move audio into the library and leave the database
# describing where the audio USED to be -- or, on the rollback side, one of the
# ways a failed row write used to leave the library holding orphan copies and
# the original demoted. Some FILEs are in internal/organizer: that is the code
# under test, but its observable behaviour (rows, primary flags, files on disk)
# is asserted from internal/server, which is what --pkg names.

# The batch-save caller stops at the file operation again: files copied into
# the library, nothing at all written to the database.
M01 batch-save-skips-the-row-write | internal/server/batch_save_op.go | s/\toutcome, _, err := s\.organizeService\.CommitLanding\(book, landing, operationID, log\)\n/\t_ = landing\n\toutcome, err := organizer.LandingVersioned, error(nil)\n/

# The folder-auto-scan op stops delegating and organizes nothing.
M02 autoscan-drops-the-organize-hook | internal/server/folder_autoscan_op.go | s/\t\t\t\ts\.autoOrganizeScannedBooks\(ctx, books, scanLog\)\n/\t\t\t\t_ = ctx\n/

# A failed row write leaves the copies it wrote in the library: orphan audio
# under the root that the next organize collides with as _copy1.
M03 rollback-keeps-the-created-copies | internal/organizer/service.go | s/\n\tRemoveCreated\(landing, newBookID, log\)\n/\n\t_ = landing\n/

# A failed row write goes on to demote the original anyway -- a version group
# whose primary owns no audio while the row that has the files is superseded.
M04 failed-row-write-still-demotes-original | internal/organizer/service.go | s/\t\t\torgSvc\.rollbackOrganizedVersion\(newBookID, landing, log\)\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt\.Errorf\("copy book files for %s: %w", book\.ID, err\)\n/\t\t\torgSvc.rollbackOrganizedVersion(newBookID, landing, log)\n/

# The rows are created at the SOURCE paths instead of the landed ones. This is
# the original defect in its purest form: right number of rows, every one of
# them naming a file the organized book does not own.
M05 rows-created-at-the-source-paths | internal/organizer/service.go | s/\t\t\t\tnewBF\.FilePath = resolveOrganizedFilePath\(bf\.FilePath, landing\.Files, log\)\n/\t\t\t\tnewBF.FilePath = bf.FilePath\n/
